__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated archives never belong in the repo -- a transcript is a verbatim
# record of a real conversation, including file paths, tool output and
# anything that was pasted into it. Archive output is ignored by extension
# everywhere, and the repository's own documents are whitelisted below.
*.html
*.txt
*.md
*.tex
*.pdf
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
missfont.log
demo/
logs/

# ...except the files the repo genuinely needs. A new root-level document has
# to be added here or it is silently never committed: `*.md` above is broad on
# purpose, and 2.8.0's SECURITY.md and translated READMEs were both caught by
# `git add` refusing them. The suite now checks that each of these is TRACKED,
# not merely present on disk, so the next one fails before a push, not after.
!README.md
!README.*.md
!AGENTS.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!SECURITY.md
!docs/*.md
!docs/*.html
!docs/*.pdf
!tests/baseline_html.txt
